[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/4a37393b74d177d5e32f06cfd097ff6eb9f507b8/src/Init/Data/List/Nat/TakeDrop.lean#L196-L198\">This</a> is <code>List.dropLast_take</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dropLast_take</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">take</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dropLast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">take</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dropLast_eq_take</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">length_take</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le_of_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">min_eq_left</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">take_take</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_le</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The hypothesis could be a weak inequality (allowing <code>i = l.length</code>) just by deleting the <code>Nat.le_of_lt</code> call before the use of <code>h</code>.</p>\n<p>Could this be fixed?</p>\n<p>(fun fact: this lemma went from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib3/pull/6380\">mathlib3</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/966\">mathlib4</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/pull/272\">Batteries</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/4059\">core</a>)</p>",
        "id": 615044438,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786038892
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a lemma that says <code>l.dropLast = l.take (l.length - 1)</code>? Because that's the simplified form when <code>i = l.length</code></p>",
        "id": 615048257,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1786039877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, there's <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.dropLast_eq_take#doc\">docs#List.dropLast_eq_take</a> which is exactly that, and also the related <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.take_eq_dropLast#doc\">docs#List.take_eq_dropLast</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.dropLast_take_eq_take_dropLast#doc\">docs#List.dropLast_take_eq_take_dropLast</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.take_length#doc\">docs#List.take_length</a>.</p>\n<p>The equality case isn't the issue, it's the off-by-one. When I have <code>i ≤ l.length</code> I can't use this lemma but I should be able to.</p>",
        "id": 615049650,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786040392
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the meantime, if you have the le, you can split on eq_or_lt and use the related lemmas.</p>",
        "id": 615050054,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1786040538
    },
